  "summary": {
    "derivative_id": "der:rc4:cb_0efc3a5d9f844ddda1a19832eb00d6ee:summary",
    "text": "Seniors Rights Service is a community legal and advocacy organisation based in Surry Hills that operates across New South Wales. It provides free, confidential legal advice and services for older people (including matters relating to strata, retirement villages, boarding houses and advance legal documents), aged care advocacy for recipients of Commonwealth-funded aged care services, targeted rights-based information and education (brochures, fact sheets and information sessions), community development including public seminars and events, and telephone advice and referral lines. The service offers dedicated support for First Nations older people, LGBTQ+ older people and older people from linguistically diverse backgrounds and lists multilingual access and referral options."
  },
